From 56dbf5d3ef8f8fde717c76dbe4dad4c533b93345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 10:47:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02548/11362] [outer-loop] M2-v2: composite (move+recolor)
 rules -- NOT reflect (measured: 0/9 games reflect)

Redirected from the requested 'reflect rule': I measured the actual per-action dynamics
across all 9 games and found ZERO reflections (every game is single-object translate +
multi/recolor, never a flipH/flipV). My earlier 'ar25 reflects' was an over-read of the
win-keyword; at the dynamics level ar25 translates. A reflect rule would have helped
nothing, so per the 'correct a misconception' discipline I built what the data demands.

THE REAL GAP (visible in the large multi/recolor transition bucket -- cd82 83, tu93 81,
m0r0 74, cn04 52): a single action often does TWO things at once -- move an object AND
recolor a HUD/selection cell -- but M2-v2 induced only ONE rule per action, so it floored
on those transitions.

THE FIX (additive, backward-compatible): a ('seq', [rule, ...]) composite rule + GREEDY
composition in fit(). Greedy starts from identity and repeatedly appends the atomic rule
(translate / translate_obj / a residual-fixing recolor_all) that best explains what the
current sequence still gets wrong, until none helps (cap length 3). _residual_recolor_cands
proposes the recolor that fixes the residual AFTER a move is applied (the old single-recolor
enumeration could not see it, because a move+recolor diff has >1 colour pair). Single-effect
actions yield a length-1 BARE rule -- byte-for-byte the prior behaviour.

ISOLATED RESULT (single-rule baseline vs composite, M2's own dynamics_accuracy):
  cn04: 0.174 -> 0.477 (+0.303)   ar25: 0.307 -> 0.379 (+0.072)
  ka59: 0.151 -> 0.215 (+0.064)   tu93: 0.228 -> 0.273 (+0.045)
  sp80: 0.651 -> 0.651 (+0.000, 0 composite actions -- back-compat, no regression)
The lift is broad and lands on exactly the multi-effect-action games. cd82 stays 0.000
(genuinely nonrigid dynamics -- not move+recolor; an honest residual hard case).

Tests: 7/7 pass (5 prior back-compat + 1 new composite, assert-bearing per CLAUDE.md);
consumer arc_execution_guided_world_model imports + tests clean (13/13 together).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
